# docviewer has no required environment variables for the deployed
# container: FILES_ROOT, DB_PATH, and CACHE_DIR are baked into the image via
# ENV in the Containerfile (FILES_ROOT=/data/files,
# DB_PATH=/data/db/docviewer.sqlite3, CACHE_DIR=/data/cache), and there is no
# session-signing secret to configure (sessions are opaque DB-backed tokens
# with nothing to sign). This file — and the
# `~/docviewer-data/docviewer.env` it's copied to for the deployed
# container — can stay empty; it exists so `EnvironmentFile=` in
# docviewer.container has something to point at, and as a place to add
# variables if you introduce ones that need overriding later.
#
# For local development without the container, uncomment and edit these to
# point at local paths (app/config.py requires all three, with no defaults):
# FILES_ROOT=./dev-data/files
# DB_PATH=./dev-data/db/docviewer.sqlite3
# CACHE_DIR=./dev-data/cache
